  summary:'The implementation covers the feature. JsonlSource reads by byte offset in tail_chunk_kb chunks, opens files read-only, keeps an unterminated trailing line until EOF (drain_partial), and exposes next_batch/at_eof as described in architecture section 4.1/4.2. The v1 mapper yields exactly one EventKind::Unknown { raw_type } per line, with <unparseable> for non-JSON or untyped lines, so the mapping is total. The mapping version comes from <slug>.capture.json via MappingVersion::for_droid_version, falling back to LATEST. observatory-cli replay prints <rfc3339>\\t<n> <lane>\\tunknown.event(<raw_type>)\\t<session> per event and the exact final line `unknown events: N`. A missing file exits 1 with the path on stderr and prints no summary line. One replay run on the S fixture: exit 0, 2028 stdout lines for 2027 fixture lines, last line `unknown events: 2027`, every event line matches the 4-field format (agent_turn_outcome 31, compaction_state 5, message 1952, session_start 1, todo_state 38), fixture sha256 unchanged, ~/.droid-observatory absent, and git status clean. The missing-file run exits 1 with `observatory-cli: cannot read fixtures/streams/nope.jsonl: No such file or directory (os error 2)`. On "children included per architecture": architecture section 4.2 heading says "JsonlSource (S; sidecar and children M0)", the section 2 M0 row assigns child discovery to M0, and VAL-SKEL-005 requires the event-line count to equal `wc -l` of the root S fixture. So counting the root file only is correct for S, and the tests (replay_s.rs:43-61, cli.rs:57-80) compare against the root file line count, which is what the contract requires. JsonlSource::add_file already exists for M0. Red-before-green order holds: 830e895 red then 69cb91e green (version), 055fc16 red then cc1fe27 green (ingest/mapping/replay_s), a959cbd red then 90215d5 green (CLI). Every unknown event is counted and shown (rule 18). No shared files (SPEC.md, README.md, BACKLOG.md, docs/decisions/README.md) were touched; the changed files are limited to Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock and the two crates. The machete ignored list still names only rusqlite, keyring-core and apple-native-keyring-store, none of which is used yet, so it correctly stays unchanged. The Makefile replay-fixtures loop already ran the real subcommand. The tests use env!("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR"), which is the standard way to locate fixtures. The earlier failures came from a stale test binary built in a deleted clone sharing CARGO_TARGET_DIR, an environment problem and not a code defect.',
