  {area:'knowledge',observation:'A shared CARGO_TARGET_DIR can hold integration-test binaries built from another checkout (for example, a deleted scratch clone) with CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR compiled in, which makes fixture-path tests fail until the test file is touched or rebuilt. The runtime-limits notes or library should record this so validators do not report a false failure.',evidence:'Parent task notes: the first scrutiny run had 3 cli.rs failures from a stale binary built in target/scratch/clone; they passed after touching crates/observatory-cli/tests/cli.rs.'},
  {area:'knowledge',observation:'The S replay output format is now fixed and could be documented for later milestones and validators: `<rfc3339 millis>\\t<lane number> <lane name>\\t<prd kind name>(<raw_type> for Unknown)\\t<session id>`, then `unknown events: N`. A broken pipe exits 0.',evidence:`${W}/crates/observatory-cli/src/replay.rs:42-57, main.rs:50-54`}
 ],
 addressesFailureFrom:null,
 summary:'Pass. JsonlSource, the Unknown-only v1 mapping with the capture-header version, and observatory-cli replay meet VAL-SKEL-004..008 and 013. One replay run printed 2027 event lines plus `unknown events: 2027`, equal to wc -l of the root fixture. Counting the root file only is correct for S per architecture section 4.2 and VAL-SKEL-005; children belong to M0. A missing file exits 1 with the path on stderr, the fixture hash is unchanged, and no store or home directory is created. The red-then-green commit order holds for all three test groups, and no shared files were edited. There are no blocking issues. The non-blocking notes are the architecture signature difference for for_droid_version and the epoch timestamp on session_start.'
};
